      {
        "changes": [
          {
            "details": "Pinned upstream quantifies disk offload at about 5 GB host RAM plus 5 GB accelerator memory versus about 36 GB host RAM plus 5 GB accelerator memory for CPU offload. The dedicated adapter preserves the exact checkpoint, Gemma closure, and output contract. Its conservative Candidate envelope subtracts only that documented 31 GB host-memory delta from the prior profile: startup 124 to 93 GB and steady 108 to 77 GB, with growth and system reserve unchanged at 8 GB each. Admission therefore requires 101 GB including reserve and fits a 128 GB Spark; physical acceptance and refinement remain pending.",
